  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health Policy and Systems Research to inform emergency preparedness in fragile, conflict-affected and vulnerable (FCV) settings</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A collaboration between the World Health Organization (WHO) Alliance for Health Policy and Systems Research (AHPSR) and the National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) to support a call for Health Policy and Systems research that systematically examines how and why fragile, conflict-affected, and vulnerable (FCV) settings have (or have not) been able to manage previous emergencies.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Convene national stakeholders (particularly in the Eastern Mediterranean and African regions) to identify Health Policy and Systems Research (HPSR) priorities around emergency preparedness and inform the development of a framework specific to emergency preparedness in fragile, conflict-affected and vulnerable (FCV) settings; 
Support the development of HPSR led by researchers and practitioners based in selected FCV settings to respond to the identified priorities and support national emergency preparedness efforts - to this end the research programme will specifically identify and support FCV settings where there are existing/envisaged processes to strengthen the emergency preparedness architecture;  
Draw cross-national and cross-regional learning to inform regional and global emergency preparedness efforts; and  
Strengthen capacities of selected FCV setting-based researchers and practitioners in the conduct and dissemination of HPSR.</narrative>
  </description>
